\title{Augmented global free/forgetful adjunction}
\taxon{Development}
\meta{layer}{human}
\meta{source}{Kernel/Augmented/FreeGeneratingAdjunction.lean}
\tag{foundation}
\tag{augmented}

\p{This continues \ref{augmented-generating} under \ref{dec-kr-0018} and \ref{at-fd-0007}. The global adjunction and its induced monad are checked. Monadicity is the next construction obligation.}
\p{\code{BaseMap} now has checked identities and composition, including their action on complete boundary frames. \code{CellGraph.OverMap} retains each cell with its full boundary. Its typed cell and row maps preserve incidence; the identity and composition laws are checked. \code{Operations.OverMap} adds preservation of both identities and substitution as ordinary equalities of cells with their boundaries attached. These form the checked category \code{BundledAlgebra}.}
\p{\code{BundledAlgebra.forget} is the checked functor to generating incidence graphs. Cells are sorted by their actual input and zero/one output lengths. Ordered vertex/edge getters and their path reconstruction lemmas retain every incidence, including empty boundaries. Naturality identifies a graph map's generator assignments with their complete typed boundaries.}
\p{\code{Generating.Graph.lift} extends graph maps to global algebra maps; \code{unit_lift} and \code{lift_restrictMap} prove its two inverse laws. \code{homEquiv_naturality} packages the mapping equivalence into \code{BundledAlgebra.free}, \code{freeForgetAdjunction} and \code{generatingMonad}. The unit and counit formulas are checked. The adjunction is global: objects and both kinds of arrows vary.}
\p{\code{forget} and \code{generatingComparison} are faithful. \code{comparisonHomEquiv} characterizes comparison morphisms as graph maps commuting with evaluation of every free expression. From that equation, \code{comparisonVertical} recovers vertical identity/composition preservation, and \code{comparisonCells} recovers the full boundary-preserving cell map, its graph-map round trip and evaluation factorization. Both identity-cell preservation laws are proved.}
\p{\code{generatorCell}, \code{generatorRow} and \code{generatorOuter} lift entire incident substitution inputs to free representatives. Their evaluation laws recover the original cells, shared sides and paths. \code{comparisonCells_substitute} therefore proves preservation of arbitrary substitution. \code{comparisonMap} reconstructs the augmented-algebra map and \code{forget_comparisonMap} proves its graph-map round trip. The actual comparison is fully faithful, witnessed by \code{generatingComparisonFullyFaithful}; \code{forget} also reflects isomorphisms.}
\p{\strong{Remaining:} reconstruction of an augmented algebra from an arbitrary generating-monad algebra, and the resulting essential surjectivity/comparison equivalence. Thus monadicity is not yet proved. The augmented arity theorem, its density/recognition hypotheses and labelled diagram model remain open. No gate status or statement is changed. Public map-preservation laws use ordinary equality of cells with their complete boundaries; internal typed adapters still use heterogeneous equality.}
\p{Reproduce with \code{lake build Augmented}, the foundation axiom inventory and seal/swap checks. This adds no sealed constant.}
\p{Cites: \ref{dec-kr-0015}, \ref{dec-rt-0030}, \ref{dec-wf-0008}, \ref{dec-wf-0010}.}

\p{\strong{Monad-algebra reconstruction evidence:} \ref{augmented-monad-vertical} reconstructs vertical categories and functors from arbitrary generating-monad algebras, retains the horizontal graph and proves a natural equivalence recovering each existing augmented algebra's vertical category. \ref{augmented-monad-cells} adds incident cells, all primitive operations and a surjective full-boundary evaluation map preserving both identities and arbitrary substitution. The five augmented equation families for the reconstructed operations, the comparison action identification and essential surjectivity remain open; monadicity is not yet proved.}
